    "title": "China's Premier Makes a Rare 3-day Trip to North Korea",
    "text": "Chinese Premier Li Qiang is heading to North Korea for a rare three-day visit marking the 80th anniversary of the country’s ruling party. The trip signals Beijing’s effort to strengthen ties with Pyongyang while balancing its broader relations with the U.S. and South Korea. NTD spoke with Bruce Klingner, senior fellow at the Mansfield Foundation for insight.\nChina's Premier Makes a Rare 3-day Trip to North Korea\nChinese Premier Li Qiang is heading to North Korea for a rare three-day visit marking the 80th anniversary of the country’s ruling party.\nBy\n|\nPublished: 10/8/2025, 11:58:18 PM EDT",
